  "explanation": "The question asks for the year Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus was elected consul. Multiple sources (D1S1, D1S2, D2S12, D3S1) directly state that he was consul in 112 BC. The reference to 148 BC refers to his father, also named Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus, as stated in D1S1, D2S11, and D4S1. Since the question specifies the individual in question and not his father, 112 BC is the correct and only relevant answer."
